# HAZARD: owl:intersectionOf on a NAMED class, OWL 1's way of stating
# C ≡ X ⊓ Y. The OWL 2 mapping reads intersectionOf only on an anonymous
# class expression, and HOWL once skipped this triple as a class
# expression's internals: dropped without an omission, so C ⊑ X was missed
# and the run reported coherent (W3C WebOnt-equivalentClass-004 found it).
# Expect: the triple reported as an omission, so the run is inconclusive
# (exit 2), never coherent.

@prefix :     <http://example.org/t#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .

<http://example.org/t> a owl:Ontology .
:C a owl:Class . :X a owl:Class . :Y a owl:Class .
:C owl:intersectionOf ( :X :Y ) .
